Source provenance

The development source registry records adaptations from an upstream runtime
supplied during development, including shared frontmatter formats; message,
session, provider and tool-host abstractions; guardrails, retry and budget
logic; LLM streaming adapters; filesystem and command tools; AgentLoop and
context compaction; plugin HookPoint definitions; goal-ledger and reflection
formats. Some implementations are trimmed or reimplemented rather than copied
verbatim. Existing source notices and authorship remain applicable; this
summary does not grant rights to upstream material or replace its terms.

The Office protocol test snapshot is separately attributed and MIT-licensed;
see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md and its retained upstream LICENSE. Historical
internal development records are retained locally. Before publishing complete
Git history, maintainers must also review upstream redistribution rights and
historical private data; removing records from the current tree does not remove
them from earlier commits.
